skill: "prior-art-search"
sections[3]:
  - "# prior-art-search\n\nRun a structured prior-art search and write the novelty report for an invention disclosure, including the trademark watch check. Use when a disclosure arrives from engineering, before any patent filing decision, or when a competitor filing needs screening against the company's roadmap.\n\nOwner: role-ip-patent-attorney (pod-gna, legal). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[5]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - search_web\n  - web_fetch\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"invention disclosure disclosure.toon (problem, elements, advantages); CPC classification hints; USPTO database access via scientific-db-uspto-database; trademark watch list tm-watch-list.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/legal/prior-art-report.toon with search_strategy[], screened_hits[], closest_art[] ranked, novelty_opinion; tm_findings[]\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Read the disclosure and extract the inventive elements as separate testable propositions; an element that cannot be tested against prior art is rewritten until it can.\n2. Propose the search strategy: classification codes, keyword sets in the field's own vocabulary, and assignee names of known competitors; the strategy is recorded before any search runs so scope is fixed.\n3. Run the searches through the USPTO database skill and search_web; log every query string and source so the search is reproducible.\n4. Screen hits against each inventive element: a reference anticipates only if every element of a claim appears in that single reference; combinations are noted as obviousness evidence, not anticipation.\n5. Rank the closest art with an element-by-element mapping table per reference; state explicitly which elements each reference misses.\n6. Run the trademark watch: screen new marks in tm-watch-list.toon against the disclosure's branding, and log classes and statuses checked.\n7. Write the novelty opinion in plain statements of what the art shows and what remains unshown; an opinion that hedges every line is returned to be rewritten, not filed.\n8. Emit ask_question to the operator only for scope questions (new elements discovered mid-search); hand prior-art-report.toon to role-general-counsel and outside counsel for the filing decision.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nnovelty opinion to role-general-counsel and outside counsel; tm findings to brand owner.\n"
